{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["And the reason for <b>חשק</b> («desire») is that He bound Himself to you with a mighty bond that shall never be separated from you forever, from the language of וחשוקיהם כסף (Exodus 27:10) («and their sockets of silver»). «And He chose you from all the peoples» — that you shall be His treasure and inheritance, for choice (ברירה) everywhere means selection from among others. And He stated the reason: «For from HaShem's love for you He chose you» — for He saw you as worthy of being beloved before Him and chosen for love more than all the peoples. And He did not mention in this any reason for the choice, for the chosen one as a beloved is one who knows how to bear everything that comes upon him from Him, and Israel are worthy of this more than any people, as the Sages said (Beitzah 25b): «Three are brazen: Israel among the nations» — for they stand firm for Him in trials; or «a Jew or a crucified one» (Shemot Rabbah 42:9). And the reason for «you» is: for the sake of your fathers, whose matter had reached the point that He swore to them, so that sin would not cause and nullify their promise; and therefore He brought you out of the land of Egypt with a mighty hand. «And He redeemed you» — this alludes that He struck them in your stead, as it is said (Isaiah 43:3): «I gave Egypt as your ransom, Cush and Seba in your stead.»"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "In the phrase 'or a Jew or a crucified one,' the citation to Shemot Rabbah 42:9 is rendered as it appears in the text; the referent of this parenthetical is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:46:34.434343645Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}